# SXT Tools demo — environment template
#
# Two demo paths, two levels of setup:
#
#   READ-ONLY DEMO (5 min, free, no wallet)
#     Set SXT_API_KEY only. Run `npm run demo` from the repo root. You'll see
#     a verified Proof of SQL query against the canonical STAKERS table —
#     same prover, same on-chain Verifier as a full pipeline run.
#
#   FULL PIPELINE (~30 min, ~$10 in SXT/ETH, requires wallet)
#     Set both PRIVATE_KEY and SXT_API_KEY. Funded wallet needed on 3 networks
#     (SXT credits, Base ETH, 100 SXT for the on-chain query). Run
#     `node bootstrap.mjs --status` to verify funding.

# READ-ONLY: Studio API key from chain.spaceandtime.io → API Authentication.
# Free signup. This single value unlocks the off-chain proof demo.
SXT_API_KEY=

# FULL PIPELINE: Ethereum private key (0x-prefixed). Used to:
#   • sign Substrate extrinsics on the SXT chain (publish + insert)
#   • sign Ethereum transactions (deploy + approve + query)
# Wallet must be funded on three networks; see `node bootstrap.mjs --status`.
# Leave empty for the read-only demo.
PRIVATE_KEY=

# Optional overrides — defaults work for most users.
# SXT_RPC=wss://rpc.mainnet.sxt.network        # SXT chain (Substrate) for publish; defaults to mainnet
# SXT_RPC_HTTP=https://rpc.mainnet.sxt.network # HTTP variant used by save-proof-plans.mjs
# ETH_RPC=https://base.publicnode.com          # EVM target for deploy + query; defaults to Base mainnet
# MAX_WAIT_MS=180000                            # query-onchain.mjs callback wait window
# ETHERSCAN_API_KEY=                            # only for index-contract.mjs --events (ABI-fetch)
#                                               # mode; --event-signature mode needs no key

# ─── SXT Toolkit overrides — point the pipeline at your own data ────────────
# With no overrides set, the demo runs against the canonical sxt_stakers
# dataset shipped in examples/data/. Set these to publish, prove, and query
# a table you own.

# SXT_TABLE=MY_PROJECT_<UPPERCASE_HEX_ADDRESS>.MY_TABLE
#   Full dotted reference to your published SXT table. Read by:
#     - save-proof-plans.mjs  (which queries to plan against)
#     - verify-table.mjs      (which table to off-chain prove against)

# SXT_POINT_LOOKUP=0x<value you expect IS in the table>
#   Value used in the positive-membership proof. For VARCHAR columns this
#   is the literal string (typically an address); for BIGINT this is a
#   numeric ID. The rendered OnchainQuery contract proves this value is a
#   member of the configured lookup column, emitting QueryRow on success.

# SXT_LOOKUP_COLUMN=COLUMN_NAME
#   Which column the membership proof checks (point-lookup query).
#   When unset, save-proof-plans.mjs auto-picks the first VARCHAR column
#   from the schema — fine if your CSV has a single string identifier
#   column. Set this when your schema has multiple VARCHAR columns and you
#   need a specific one (e.g. EMAIL vs USERNAME).

# SXT_SCHEMA_PATH=../data/<csv-base>.inferred-schema.json
#   Path to the schema JSON describing your table's columns. publish-dataset-cli.mjs
#   writes <csv-base>.inferred-schema.json next to your CSV after a successful
#   publish, so the default flow doesn't require any hand-curation. Override
#   here only if you keep hand-curated schemas elsewhere.

# SAMPLE_STAKER=0x<same idea, used by verify-table.mjs off-chain>
#   Defaults to the demo's known staker. Override to test your own data.
